		)
		(uuid "00e0a621-b3a7-4dec-a6b5-c863f8c69418")
	)
	(text "R110 10k / R111 3.3k set the PowerGood window together with the firmware constants PGOOD_DIV_LO_MV / PGOOD_DIV_HI_MV in main.c. The firmware does not know the divider\nratio at run time: it compares the measured voltage against mV values pre-computed from 3.3/13.3 = 0.24812. Changing these resistors without recomputing both constants\nshifts the trip points silently - no error is raised. 1% parts are required. The firmware window is 8.0-12.0 V (nominal); worst-case unit tolerance of +-2.6% (+-1.5%\nfrom the 1% divider) can move the trips to 8.21 V / 11.69 V, leaving 0.19 V of margin to the specified 8.4-11.5 V operating range. With 5% parts (divider +-7.5%)\nwarnings can fire inside that range. At 12 V the divider gives 2.977 V, 0.3 V below VDDA. Raising the ratio saturates the ADC and the upper trip stops working."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 226.06 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0f59a3e4-2136-424f-a08a-5c83b0bab748")
	)
	(text "BOOT0 is pulled low by a 10k to ensure \nboot from the internal Flash memory."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 226.314 28.448 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "17bb4b3a-78aa-4e1b-91be-40997c983a54")
	)
	(text "MIDI-Learn"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 201.676 42.418 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3061168a-2181-42de-9aa4-ece849cbe805")
	)
	(text "Because the NJW4191's output contains significant switching noise (80mVpp 141kHz triangular ripple), \na ripple filter is required at its output."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
